# Slack notify on finished updates

After you **finish adding updates** to this project (gameplay, assets, docs, hosting, rules, or other repo changes), **post to Slack `#city-builder` before you end the turn**. Do this every time. Do not wait for the user to ask.

## Channel

- Name: `#city-builder`
- Channel ID: `C0BQC5201PV`
- Tool: Slack MCP `slack_send_message` (send the message; do not leave it as a draft)

## When to post

Post when the turn produced a real update: commits, new features, README/docs, assets, tests, or configuration.

Do **not** post for question-only turns with no repo changes (for example “how does X work?” with no edits).

## What to say

Keep it short and useful as a notification:

- One-line what shipped
- How to try it (`npm run dev` → http://localhost:5173, or any live URL)
- PR or commit if one exists (`https://github.com/Mahonri-Ryi/exploration/pull/2`)

Set `unfurl_app_links` to true when the message includes the GitHub PR.

Return the Slack message link in your user-facing summary.
